league/runner/README.md:1067:RU-PremierLeague has joined with SOT (GZ) and total shots (arm B). RU-PremierLeague has joined with SOT (GZ — Gate Zero; PROVISIONAL PASS, virgin calibration −4.07pp within one standard error of 3.11pp; primary 8.5, ladder 7.5/8.5/9.5, halves share 0.4612, div RU-PremierLeague, ratio prior 200, 1H ladder 3.5/4.5/5.5, 2H ladder 4.5/5.5/6.5) and total shots (arm B, PROVISIONAL PASS, virgin calibration −2.59pp within one standard error of 3.09pp; primary 25.5, ladder 24.5/25.5/26.5, halves share 0.4602, 1H ladder 11.5/12.5/13.5, 2H ladder 13.5/14.5/15.5) — read from the frozen preregs and verdicts and cross-checked against the shipped virgin predictions. Goals (FAIL at dev), corners, and cards failed their gates and are excluded. The arm-B dispatch needed no extension: the runner's predict_total_shots_arm_b (the SCO-Premiership precedent) calls exactly the composition RU ships — RU's total-shots model.py is identical to SCO's except its docstring (same M_BAR 24.9) — and RU's fitted_params.json carries every field the dispatch reads (lambda 30.0, r_A 91.2360, level cell [30, 0.5, 50], ladder 24.5/25.5/26.5, half split [0.4602, 0.5398]): the registered lines and constant, not the defective shipped-format writer values the league build bypassed (a 25.5/26.5/27.5 FT ladder and a stale 0.4592 half split from another league); the recompute below is the arbiter and it reproduces the runner. The SOT engine needed no change: it already accepts the runner's ratio_prior keyword (the AU pattern), and the coordinator verified the runner's ratio_prior=200 construction is bitwise-identical to the no-arg engine. The data builder needed two fixes: its frozen 1,312-match count was a hard equality — a bug for a league whose 2026/2027 season is still running — now a floor, and it ignored the runner's INDEX/MAIN_REPO globals (it read the index from a hard-coded main-checkout root via argparse); it now follows the runner contract, with the explicit CLI override preserved. The builder encodes missing values as empty fields: there are no 'nan' strings anywhere in either CSV, the SOT and total-shots adapter columns are complete on all 1,312 rows, and no name in either CSV is non-ASCII (FotMob's Russian team and referee names are Latin transliterations; the payloads' only non-ASCII characters are Latin-extended player-name letters that never reach the CSVs), so encoding round-trips through the runner's UTF-8 readers exactly. RU-PremierLeague is a world league (Russia, Premier League, FotMob id 63) over seasons 2021/2022–2026/2027, a clean 240-match double round-robin per complete season (1,312 matches and 2,624 team rows at the join: five complete seasons plus 112 played in 2026/2027); at the 2026-11-09 join, FotMob listed exactly the remaining 128 fixtures of 2026/2027 (from 2026-11-20), all predicted in both markets with zero errors, and nothing settled (every ledger entry is a future fixture). An independent recompute of the first fixture (5847235, FC Rostov–Krylya Sovetov Samara, 2026-11-20) from the engine code alone matched all 18 daily-CSV fields with max difference 0.0 in each market, and a synthetic settlement on match 5847230 (Zenit St. Petersburg–FC Rostov, 2026-11-08) graded SOT actual 8.0 and total-shots actual 22.0 correctly, settled each market exactly once (a second pass settled nothing), and left the artifacts md5-clean. Two end-to-end proof runs on 2026-11-09 (29 leagues, 68 markets) each completed with zero errors and fetched nothing new in any league in either run (9,612 predictions in run 1, 9,606 in run 2); every output was bit-identical between the runs (215 compared files) except ES-LaLiga2's three daily CSVs, because FotMob's LaLiga2 listing dropped two fixtures dated 2026-11-09 (Las Palmas–Eldense and Sabadell–Real Sociedad B) between the runs — 321 upcoming in run 1, 319 in run 2, and neither was fetched as a result — while RU's outputs were bit-identical. The completed runs followed five attempts lost to infrastructure under heavy parallel load on this box: three OOM kills (exit 137) at the NL-Eredivisie stage (whose builder retains every parsed payload in memory), one VM reboot at about 20:38 UTC that also wiped /tmp, and one further OOM kill after the reboot; the successful runs were launched detached with MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 on the runner process, which changes no output.
