league/runner/README.md:1236:RU-1Division has joined with corners only (arm `gate_zero`, PROVISIONAL PASS in `reports/C_RU1_VERDICT.md`: virgin LL 0.698888 at the primary 8.5 line, calibration +3.28pp with the 2.28pp excess over the 1.0pp boundary within one standard error of 2.97pp; dev LL 0.695540 beat both baselines). Goals, SOT, cards, and total shots failed their gates and are excluded. Corners configuration is primary 8.5, ladder 7.5/8.5/9.5, and `halves_share_1h: null` — this league's feed has no period splits at all (`has_period_splits_content` is 0 on all 1,757 built rows, and its frozen config and shipped virgin predictions are FT-only), so it is the first user of the FT-only corners opt-in documented above: the runner writes the halves columns empty, in the same positions as every other corners league, and predicts the FT ladder only. The corners engine is the possession-only Gate Zero variant (the big-chance half of the RU-Premier pair is absent from every payload here; its fit grid hard-codes the 8.5 primary, as the reference cores do), and its `fit_params`/`model_prediction`/`over_prob` signatures match the adapter exactly, so no engine change was needed. The data builder needed the RU-Premier fixes: its frozen 1,756-match count was a hard equality — now a floor, because season sizes vary (380 in 2021/2022, 306 in each of the next three seasons, 305 in 2025/2026) and 2026/2027 is still running — and it ignored the runner's INDEX/MAIN_REPO globals; it now follows the runner contract, with the explicit CLI override preserved. The builder encodes missing values as empty fields: there are no 'nan' strings in either CSV, corners are empty on 89 score-only rows (dropped by the adapter, never imputed), the builder keeps FotMob's `BallPossesion` casing, and no team name is non-ASCII, so encoding round-trips exactly. RU-1Division is a world league (Russia, `1. Division`, FotMob id 338) over seasons 2021/2022–2026/2027 (1,757 matches and 3,514 team rows at the join: five complete seasons plus 154 played in 2026/2027); at the 2026-11-09 join, FotMob listed the remaining 152 fixtures of 2026/2027 (from 2026-11-14), all predicted in corners with zero errors, and nothing settled (every ledger entry is a future fixture; the ledger holds 152 entries with no duplicate (market, match_id, run_date) key). An independent recompute of the first fixture (5897681, Volga Ulyanovsk–Torpedo Moscow, 2026-11-14) from the engine code alone matched all four FT fields with max difference 0.0 and confirmed all eight halves fields empty (live fit gamma 0.15, r 1.4546, beta [0.0], fit_n 1,658), and a synthetic settlement on match 5897664 (FC Yenisey Krasnoyarsk–PFC Sochi, 2026-11-08) graded corners actual 9.0 correctly on the FT line, settled exactly once (a second pass settled nothing), and left the artifacts md5-clean. Two end-to-end proof runs on 2026-11-09 (33 leagues, 75 markets) each completed with zero errors and 10,682 predictions; the first run fetched exactly one match — RU-1Division's 5897663 (Veles Moscow–KamAZ, played 2026-11-09), the new league's first-ever pull — and the second run fetched nothing new in any league; every output was bit-identical between the runs (344 compared files, including both FotMob indexes), so the FT-only amendment changed no pre-existing league's numbers. The first run's first attempt was lost to a VM reboot at about 22:28 UTC after 27 of 33 leagues and was rerun in full; the completed runs were made with `MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2` on the runner process, which changes no output.
