league/runner/README.md:2017:NO-OBOSLigaen has joined with corners only (arm `gate_zero`, PROVISIONAL PASS in `reports/C_NO_OBOS_VERDICT.md`: virgin LL 0.6898 at the primary 10.5 line, calibration +1.14pp with the 0.14pp excess over the 1.0pp boundary within one standard error of 3.24pp; dev LL 0.6969 beat both baselines, league base rate 0.7257 and naive trailing-10 0.7205; Gate Zero and PLAIN tied exactly on the virgin window — the virgin fit chose beta [0.0], so the possession multiplier is inactive and the two arms are identical — and the frozen tie rule ships the simpler arm, Gate Zero). Goals, SOT, cards, and total shots failed their gates or were not buildable and are excluded. Corners configuration is primary 10.5, ladder 9.5/10.5/11.5, and `halves_share_1h: null` — this league's feed has no period splits at all (its frozen config has `corners_1h_share: null` and the shipped virgin predictions are FT-only), so it uses the FT-only corners opt-in documented above (RU-1Division precedent): the runner writes the halves columns empty and predicts the FT ladder only. The data builder needed no change: its only count assert is `len(rows) == len(idx)`, a self-consistent check that grows with the index rather than a frozen build-time count, so there is no AU/MLS trap to floor. NO-OBOSLigaen is a world league (Norway, `OBOS-ligaen`, FotMob id 203) over calendar-year seasons 2021–2026 (1,440 matches and 2,880 team rows at the join: six complete 240-match seasons; the virgin is the complete 2026 season, 237 matches with a corners target); at the 2026-11-10 join FotMob listed no upcoming fixtures (the 2026 season ended 2026-11-08 and 2027 is not requested), so nothing was predicted and nothing settled — the daily corners CSV is header-only and the ledger holds no entries. An independent recompute through the real runner adapter reproduced the shipped virgin predictions exactly: the fit on the pre-virgin window (2021–2025) reproduces `fitted_params_virgin.json` bit-for-bit (gamma 0.15, r 1.165312214160854, beta [0.0], fit_n 1,080), and the apply replay over all 237 fixtures on 66 dates matched mu and all three ladder lines with max difference 0.0 and confirmed all halves fields empty. The production live refit on full history (2021–2026) keeps gamma 0.15 and beta [0.0] with r 1.1671928089114483 (fit_n 1,317); its predictions on the virgin fixtures differ by at most 0.0002 in p_over, which is the runner's by-design daily refit, not a defect — no adapter change to `run_daily.py` was needed. A synthetic settlement on match 5105318 (Sandnes Ulf–Åsane, 2026-11-08) graded corners actual 15.0 correctly on the FT line (live prediction exp_total 11.0629, P(over 10.5) 0.5379, chosen over, hit, log loss 0.62), settled exactly once (a second pass settled nothing), and left the artifacts md5-clean. Two end-to-end proof runs on 2026-11-10 (43 leagues; 92 markets in run 1, 95 in run 2) each produced 11,957 predictions; run 1 fetched 74,852 matches (a fresh worktree with an empty warehouse) with exactly one error row — CO-PrimeraA's league step, see below — and run 2 fetched nothing new in any league with zero errors. Of 366 compared files, 363 were bit-identical between the runs, including every NO-OBOSLigaen output; the exceptions are BR-SerieB's corners and SOT daily CSVs and ZA-PSL's corners daily CSV. ZA-PSL's FT values are bit-equal to run 1's ledger on all 160 fixtures (max difference 0.0), so its delta is confined to non-ledger fields, as documented for that league. BR-SerieB differs on a single fixture, 5190810 (São Bernardo–Athletic Club MG): FotMob rescheduled it from 2026-11-14 in run 1's pull to 2026-11-12 in run 2's pull — the ledger records the run-1 date — and the fixture date anchors both models' decay/refit computation, so SOT exp_total moved 8.48895 to 8.48875 (p_over shifts at most 0.000013, no side flip) and corners mu moved 1.4e-14; the other 13 fixtures in each market are bit-identical. CO-PrimeraA's six files appear only in run 2: it failed in run 1 because its builder also reads Primera B warehouse JSONs, which no runner league pulls and a fresh worktree lacks — a pre-existing cross-league warehouse dependency, not caused by this join; the Primera B files were populated from the main checkout's warehouse (no code change) and CO then rebuilt and predicted cleanly in run 2 (0 upcoming, 0 predicted). The proof pair took four launches: run 1 completed at the first attempt, and run 2's first attempt was cut short by a service restart two leagues in, its second was OOM-killed (exit 137) at the AR-LigaProfesional stage under heavy parallel load on this box, and its third completed. All completed runs were made with `MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2`, which changes no output.
