league/runner/README.md:2312:US-USLLeagueOne has joined with corners (arm `gate_zero`, PROVISIONAL PASS in `reports/C_USLL1_VERDICT.md`: dev pooled LL@9.5 0.684403 vs league base 0.693505 and naive trailing-10 0.691119, n=486, 2022-2024 regular; virgin 2025 LL@9.5 0.688533 vs base 0.697479; calibration +1.490pp, breach within 1 SE of 3.441pp; the X7 box-touch arm failed its dev gate outright at 0.714615 and is excluded) and total shots (arm `B`, PROVISIONAL PASS in `reports/T_USLL1_VERDICT.md`: dev gate pool 2023-2024, n=321: B 0.679305 vs league base 0.694009 and naive 0.684291; virgin 2025 LL@24.5 B 0.693325 vs league base 0.696400, lowest of the three arms; calibration +2.866pp, breach within 1 SE of 3.444pp; arm C fails the dev-sign leg vs A (0/2) and is excluded; arm A is provisional but B has the lower virgin LL). Goals, SOT and cards failed their gates and are excluded. Corners configuration is primary 9.5, ladder 8.5/9.5/10.5, halves share 0.469, 1H ladder 3.5/4.5/5.5, 2H ladder 4.5/5.5/6.5; total-shots configuration is primary 24.5, ladder 23.5/24.5/25.5, halves share 0.461, 1H ladder 10.5/11.5/12.5, 2H ladder 12.5/13.5/14.5. Both markets set the new `exclude_phases: ["playoff"]` opt-in: the league's frozen phase rule excludes playoff rows from every fitting/scoring window (both engines' load functions drop non-regular rows), and the runner adapters previously included them — without the opt-in the corners fit on the pre-virgin window flips to gamma 0.0, beta [0.0025, 0.0], fit_n 665 (vs the frozen gamma 0.15, beta [0.0, 0.0], fit_n 643), and the total-shots arm-B replay sits 0.69 in mu off the shipped file. With the opt-in the fit reproduces the frozen `fitted_params_virgin.json` bit-for-bit and the total-shots replay residual is the adapter's date-grouped state only (see below). The opt-in is default-inert and mirrors the `exclude_seasons` precedent: SCO-Premiership corners and US-USLChampionship total shots arm B (84 playoff rows in its history) produce bit-identical adapter output before and after the change when the key is absent, and SCO corners is unchanged even with the key set (it has no playoff rows), while USLChampionship arm B moves on all 375 probe rows when the key is set, proving the opt-in engages (no other league's config sets the key, so no other league's behaviour changes). The data builder's frozen 1,174-match count is now a floor (`len(rows)>=1174`), so a daily rebuild survives the next played match being appended; every rebuild in the proof produced exactly 1,174 matches and 2,348 team rows. US-USLLeagueOne is a world league (USA, `USL League One`, FotMob id 9296) over calendar-year seasons 2021-2026. An independent recompute through the frozen engines reproduced both shipped virgin predictions from the rebuilt data: corners exactly (max difference 0.0 on mu, r and all nine ladder lines over all 210 rows, and the refit on the pre-virgin window reproduces `fitted_params_virgin.json` bit-for-bit), total shots to 1.7e-9 (float repr); the total-shots `fitted_params.json` values match the virgin file's arm-B values exactly (lambda 300.0, r_A 117.1426320116539, level cell [60, 1.0, 20], half split [0.461, 0.539]). The replay through the runner adapters differs only by named, by-design causes: corners max |mu| difference 1.384 (max |p_over| 0.170 at the 9.5 line) because the replay device truncates history at 2024-12-31 while the shipped file's features include earlier-2025 matches — the first-date fixtures match exactly (diff 0.0) and the gap grows through the season as within-2025 history accumulates — and total shots max |mu| difference 0.371 (max |p_over| 0.027) because the adapter defers state updates to end of day while the total-shots harness consumes same-day earlier matches (a date-grouped-harness variant reproduces the adapter value exactly); in production the adapters see complete history up to each fixture date, so neither gap is a production defect. Note the brief's claim that `predict_corners` pins the fit to `fitted_params_virgin.json` is incorrect: the runner live-fits every corners league (verified: no such code exists, `git log -S fitted_params_virgin` on `run_daily.py` is empty), and the live refit on full history (all regular rows 2021-2026) keeps gamma 0.15 but moves r to 1.1255 and beta to [0.0025, 0.025] (fit_n 1,131), shifting the virgin fixtures' mu by at most 1.40 and p_over at 9.5 by at most 0.167 — the runner's by-design daily refit, as for NO-OBOSLigaen, not a defect, and no pinning mechanism was added. Two end-to-end proof runs on 2026-11-10 (45 leagues; 99 markets): run 1 produced 12,197 predictions with 54,492 matches fetched (fresh worktree) and zero errors; run 2 produced 12,227 predictions with fetched_new=0 in every league and zero errors. The proof pair took five launches: run 1's first attempt was killed by a runtime restart at league 12/45 (after fetching 20,281 matches, zero errors) and its completed restart ran clean; run 2's first attempt was killed by a service-restart SIGTERM at league 41/45 (fetched 0, 11,885 predictions, zero errors), its second attempt was OOM-killed (exit 137) at league 7/45 while the wt-runner49 agent's full run shared the box, and its third attempt completed cleanly (overlapping the wt-runner50 agent's run, which also finished). The run-1 md5 snapshot was lost when the restarts wiped /tmp, so the run-1/run-2 file comparison was recovered through the ledgers, as the brief's exception clause allows: all 12,197 non-CO rows are bit-equal on exp_total, every FT ladder p_over and date against run 1's ledger entries (exact float equality, 0 mismatches, 0 rows without a ledger entry), and USLL1's halves recompute exactly from exp_total with the live corners r and the frozen total-shots r_A. The sole fixture-set difference is CO-PrimeraA: 0 predicted in run 1, 10 per market in run 2 (FotMob published the 2026-11-12 matchday between 16:37 and 18:14) — new rows, not changed values; its pre-copied Primera B warehouse files meant the known fresh-worktree trap never fired. At the join FotMob listed exactly one upcoming USLL1 fixture, the 2026 final on 2026-11-15 (Charlotte Independence vs Boise, match 1000023200), predicted in both markets in both runs (corners exp_total 8.8729, P(over 9.5) 0.3967; total shots exp_total 29.0744, P(over 24.5) 0.7694), and nothing settled (the final is in the future). A synthetic settlement on the latest finished match, the 2026-11-09 semi-final 1000023079 (Charlotte Independence vs Forward Madison FC), graded both markets correctly through the real adapters and settle path (corners live exp_total 9.4832, P(over 9.5) 0.4722, chosen under, actual 6.0, hit, log loss 0.6391; total shots live exp_total 27.0347, P(over 24.5) 0.6572, chosen over, actual 26.0, hit, log loss 0.4197), settled exactly once per market (a second pass settled nothing), matched an independent recompute, and left every artifact md5-clean after the synthetic entries were removed. All completed runs were made with `MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2`, which changes no output. Defects found (pre-existing, not changed by this join): the frozen builder's phase rule keys off the FotMob league name ending in "Playoff", so the six 2026 playoff matches (quarter-finals 2026-10-30/11-02 and semi-finals 2026-11-08/09, round names "Championship - Quarter-finals/Semi-finals") are flagged "regular" and enter the production fit and state, while the 29 properly-flagged 2021-2025 playoff rows are excluded — bounded impact (6 of 1,174 rows), and the coming final will be flagged the same way when played; and the entry's `warehouse:` field says "United States/USL League One" while the runner pulls with `country: USA` into "USA/USL League One" — cosmetic only, since world leagues never read the `warehouse:` field (only the J-League rebuild path does).
