league/runner/README.md:2402:AE-ProLeague has joined with total shots (arm `C`, PROVISIONAL PASS in `reports/T_AE_VERDICT.md`: dev pooled n=545 LL@25.5 A 0.682015, B 0.682259, C 0.681906 vs league base 0.696534 and naive 0.695637, all three arms passing dev; virgin 2025/2026 n=182 arm C LL@25.5 0.686302 — lowest of the three arms (A 0.687007, B 0.687541) and below league base 0.691060; calibration breach +3.10pp (actual−predicted −3.10pp; the virgin season ran cold on shots, 24.48/match vs 25.67–26.87 dev, so every arm overstates the over-rate), inside 1 SE (3.67pp) of the 1.0pp boundary — legs (i) and (iii) PASS, leg (ii) PROVISIONAL. Both-pass rule: A and C pass all legs; the lower pooled virgin LL ships → arm C. Arm B is excluded (fails leg (i) vs A). Goals, SOT, corners and cards failed their gates and are excluded. Total-shots configuration is primary 25.5, ladder 24.5/25.5/26.5, halves share 0.4608, 1H ladder 10.5/11.5/12.5, 2H ladder 12.5/13.5/14.5. No `exclude_seasons`: the frozen harness fits on all seasons (2021/2022 is the tuning seed, scored from 2022/2023), and the adapter reads `trailing_r_window` 200 from `fitted_params.json` as designed — no block key was added for it. Two changes were needed. The data builder's frozen-count asserts are now floors (completed seasons stay exact at 182 each, the in-progress 2026/2027 season `>= 49`, total `>= 959`), following the AU/MLS/USLL1 trap precedent, so a daily rebuild survives new 2026/2027 results. And the runner's total-shots arm-C path now falls back to the market's frozen `halves_share_1h` when `fitted_params.json` carries no `half_split` — AE is the first arm-C league without one (all six existing arm-C leagues carry it; the unamended adapter raised `KeyError: 'half_split'` on the first replay attempt), mirroring the arm-A (CL-LigaDePrimera) and arm-B (CN-SuperLeague) fallback precedent. Inertness was proven on GR-SuperLeague, the natural probe (same arm C, `half_split` present): `predict_total_shots_arm_c` run with the HEAD version of `run_daily.py` and with the amended version on identical inputs produced byte-identical output on all 8 fixed pseudo-upcoming fixtures. The independent recompute of the shipped virgin predictions (182 rows, arm C) reproduces the verdict exactly from the CSV itself (LL@25.5 0.686302, breach +3.10pp); replaying them through the runner adapter differs by max |mu| 0.0210 (mean 0.0027) and max |p_over@25.5| 0.00148, replay LL@25.5 0.686260 — and the gap is fully decomposed, not assumed: re-running the replay with the 2 awarded matches removed from history (the frozen harness drops them; the runner adapter includes them, pre-existing uniform adapter behaviour, not changed by this join) reproduces the shipped file to max |mu| 1.8e-07, so the entire replay difference is the awarded-rows effect on the live refit. Fitted params: lambda 300.0, r_A 156.5851, level cell [120.0, 0.5, 50.0], trailing window 200. Two full end-to-end proof runs on 2026-11-10 (VM date; 2026-11-11 WIB) — 49 leagues, 12,418 predictions each, zero errors in either run; run 2 fetched nothing new in any league. Both runs completed first try with `MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2` (run 1 ~34 min, run 2 ~32 min) despite the SK-1Liga join proof run and the final Codex-sol audit sharing the box — no kills, no restarts, no retries. Of 250 snapshotted output files (daily CSVs, ledgers, settled-keys sidecars, grading ledgers), 249 are bit-identical between the runs, including every AE-ProLeague output; the sole exception is ZA-PSL's corners daily CSV, the known pre-existing case — its FT values are bit-equal to run 1's ledger on all 160 fixtures (max difference 0.0 on exp_total and all 480 ladder p_over values), so its delta is confined to non-ledger fields. Unlike the last joins, AE-ProLeague predicted real fixtures on day one: 70 upcoming 2026/2027 fixtures in both runs (2026-11-19 to 2027-02-21), first 2026-11-19 Al-Wasl–Hatta (match 1000022240, exp_total 26.9833, P(over 25.5) 0.5816); exp_total spans 24.3319–28.5102, the 1H share is exactly 0.4608 on all 70 rows, the ledger holds 70 entries, and nothing has settled yet (all fixtures are in the future). It is a world league (United Arab Emirates, `Pro League`, FotMob id 538) over split-year seasons 2021/2022–2026/2027, 14 teams, straight double round-robin, no play-offs; at the join the rebuild held 959 matches (182 per completed season, 49 played in 2026/2027). Two environment items: this worktree arrived without the `data_enrichment/fotmob_world` symlink the other runner worktrees carry, so the symlink to the main checkout's warehouse was restored (git-ignored, no commit impact) before the proof runs; and the CO-PrimeraA fresh-worktree trap did not trigger — its builder also reads Primera B warehouse JSONs, which are present via the symlinked main-checkout warehouse, so CO rebuilt and predicted 10 fixtures per market in both runs with no copy and no code change. Run 1's only fetch was J1's 2,092 matches into the fresh worktree's J-League store; AE fetched nothing new in either run.
